{"resourceIdentifier":"2373","resourceName":"Yellow Ipê Grouped REDD Project","description":"The Yellow Ipê Grouped REDD Project is located in the municipalities of Novo Aripuanã and Borba, south of Amazonas state, in the Northern region of Brazil. The Trans Amazonian Highway BR 230 is located in the south of the project region and, along its route, cattle raising can be found, which is one of the many agents to deforestation in the region.\r\n\r\nThe primary objective of the Yellow Ipê Grouped REDD Project is to avoid unplanned deforestation (AUD) of a specific region within the municipalities of Novo Aripuanã and Borba. The first Project activity instance has an area of 86,091.66 ha, as it is part of two private properties in Novo Aripuanã, consisting of 100% Amazon rainforest. However, other REDD project instances can be added into this grouped project activity in the future, as long as they comply with the eligibility criteria defined by the methodology and of the VCS Standard.\r\n\r\nBesides the ecological and carbon benefits of the project, a proportion of the carbon credits generated will be dedicated to improving social and environmental conditions for the local community around the project area, specifically contributing to environmental education and other social activities. The contribution to sustainability is being monitored applying the SOCIALCARBON® Standard, which is based on six key indicators: Biodiversity; Natural; Financial; Human; Social and Carbon Resources.\r\n\r\nThis REDD project is expected to avoid a predicted 27,228.38 ha of deforestation, equating to around 16,205,376 tCO2e in emissions reductions over the 30 year project lifetime (01-March-2020 to 28-February-2050).","location":{"latitude":-5.628332,"longitude":-59.686387},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2020-11-27","endExclusive":"2020-12-28","endInclusive":"2020-12-27"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2373"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Amazonas"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ecológica Assessoria Ltda."},{"type":"string","value":"Tocantins, Brazil"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2373"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2373"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"540179"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":3664}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"REDD"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0015"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"86092 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"RINA Services S.p.A"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"14/12/2021"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 01/03/2020 - 28/02/2050"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=49160&IDKEY=L0e98hfalksuf098fnsdalfkjfoijmn4309JLKJFjlaksjfla9067791640","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS Draft PD Yellow IpC_ Grouped REDD Project_v01.pdf","uploadDate":"2020-10-29T20:11:51.637Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=49161&IDKEY=8q934lkmsad39asjdkfj90qlkalsdkngaf98ulkandDfdvDdfhs67793019","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"VCS-Listing-Representation-Multiple-Representors-v4.1.pdf","uploadDate":"2020-10-29T20:13:00.577Z"}]},{"code":